# Python / editor artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.log
*.err
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Chinese-language companion of the module README.  The repository is kept in
# English only; this file is a local reading aid and is not version controlled.
negative_sampling/README.zh-CN.md
diffierent_classifical/README.zh-CN.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Superseded top-level performance outputs (kept out of version control)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/results/
/feature_batches/
/smiles/missed_drugs.csv
/targets/missed_targets.csv

# Runtime outputs of the originally published pipeline:
#   feature_batches/  the HDF5 batches written by performance/feature.py
#   model_results/    the directory that performance/model.py writes into
# The retained results of the original study are kept under
# reference_results/ and are version controlled.
performance/feature_batches/
performance/model_results/

# The same feature_batches/ directory also holds the weighted target-combination
# index (about 58 MB) and the train-only knowledge-graph artefacts of the
# classifier benchmark; they are rebuilt by features.py and are therefore not
# version controlled either.  The two result files under benchmark_results/ are
# version controlled.
performance/feature_batches/
performance/model_results/

# The classifier benchmark keeps its own intermediates in
# diffierent_classifical/feature_batches/: the weighted target-combination
# index together with the train-only knowledge-graph artefacts it contains.
# They are rebuilt by features.py and are therefore not version controlled.
# The two result files under diffierent_classifical/benchmark_results/ are
# version controlled.
/diffierent_classifical/feature_batches/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# negative_sampling: the three strategy blocks.
#   process/<block>/features/*.npy  the 3,840-dimensional pair feature matrices
#                                   (about 0.5 GB per split) exceed the 100 MB
#                                   per-file limit of the Git hosting service.
#                                   The pair metadata, the sampling manifest with
#                                   the SHA-256 fingerprints of every input, the
#                                   labels and the per-seed metrics are version
#                                   controlled, so the experiment stays auditable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/negative_sampling/process/*/features/train.npy
/negative_sampling/process/*/features/val.npy
/negative_sampling/process/*/features/test.npy

# Upstream frozen features of the cold-start regimes; they are the input of
# the negative-sampling blocks and are rebuilt by build_fold_features.py.
# Listed explicitly, because cold_start/entity_split_data/features/ holds the
# drug-level inputs that must stay under version control.
/cold_start/single_cold_start/features/train.npy
/cold_start/single_cold_start/features/val.npy
/cold_start/single_cold_start/features/test.npy
/cold_start/dual_cold_start/features/train.npy
/cold_start/dual_cold_start/features/val.npy
/cold_start/dual_cold_start/features/test.npy
/cold_start/warm_start/features/train.npy
/cold_start/warm_start/features/val.npy
/cold_start/warm_start/features/test.npy

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# baseline_experiments: regenerable artefacts.
#   data/split_data/*.npy  - the pair-level feature matrices (about 0.9 GB for
#                             the training split) and the drug-level feature
#                             arrays exceed the 100 MB per-file limit of the
#                             Git hosting service.  The pair metadata, the fold
#                             definition and the identifier tables stay under
#                             version control, so the experiment remains fully
#                             auditable; see data/split_data/README.md.
#   work/fold_features/    - per-fold feature cache, rebuilt on demand.
# The pair metadata, the fold definitions, the predictions and the result
# tables are version controlled on purpose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/baseline_experiments/data/split_data/*.npy
/baseline_experiments/data/warm_data/
/baseline_experiments/work/fold_features/
/baseline_experiments/work/*.log
/baseline_experiments/work/*.err
/baseline_experiments/work/_*.py
/baseline_experiments/work/run_remaining.ps1
/baseline_experiments/work/_backup_before_strip/
/baseline_experiments/flame
